  "slug": "dismutase-history-horizon-d1a8",
  "summary": "A review of plant superoxide dismutase history meets new work on peroxide control of germination and peroxiredoxin-driven PSII recovery.",
  "synthesis": "The items converge on reactive oxygen species (ROS) homeostasis as a regulatory axis in plants. A review traces plant superoxide dismutase research from 1969, covering ROS detoxification, compartment evolution and stress markers. Preprints extend this framework to specific contexts. Peroxisomal H2O2 homeostasis during PEG-induced water stress rebalances ABA and GA metabolism to slow Arabidopsis seed germination. Separately, 2-Cys peroxiredoxins interact with chloroplast FAD7/FAD8 desaturases to increase phosphatidylglycerol trienoic fatty acids that aid PSII recovery from high light. A published study of melatonin and selenium nanoparticles in soybean addresses salt stress through MAPK signaling, hormone balance and membrane lipid remodeling, a related but distinct stress-response thread. The shared advance is the linkage of redox state to hormone and lipid metabolism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
